From e2a43f17ed9b43ac68a7eef45f1858d45ef3ad83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Lemay <thewhiterhino1420@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:59:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat(agent): auto-reroute image turns to alternate vision
 models

When a vision-capable model is configured but the active route returns
'No endpoints found that support image input', automatically recover
by switching to image_model_fallbacks or any multimodal model in the
model list instead of failing the turn.

- recoverVisionRouting: picks first viable alternate model, resolves
  provider, swaps active candidate, emits AgentLLMRetry event
- modelConfigLooksVisionCapable: heuristic for gpt-4o/gpt-4.1/gpt-5,
  claude-3+/opus/sonnet-4, gemini, vision, multimodal, vl
- visionUnsupportedModelError: clearer guidance naming image_model and
  image_model_fallbacks
- tests: reroute to fallback model carries media refs and returns result
---
